\section{URL enumeration}{

The portal proxies raw Elasticsearch Query DSL: a \code{POST} to
\verb{https://www.ymparisto.fi/fi/app/search/query} with a JSON body. The
handler filters to \code{{"query":{"term":{"type":"yva_project"}}}} and paginates
with ES \code{from} / \code{size} against a stable \code{sort} (\verb{[\{"id":"asc"\}]}). The
~1,334 YVA records sit comfortably under the 10,000 \code{max_result_window}, so
simple from-paging covers the whole register. \code{hits.total.value} carries the
count; each result is a \verb{hits.hits[]._source} object. A free-text \code{query} is
added as a \code{bool.must} \code{match} on \code{content} + \code{title}. The proxy is an open
passthrough that returns a Drupal HTTP 500 on a malformed body, so only
read-shaped queries (\code{query} / \code{from} / \code{size} / \code{sort}) are sent and every
parse is defensive.
